# size: 360x240
# The counter's own headline value fits inside the smallest window the host
# permits, without relying on the window-scroll fallback to reveal it. This
# guards the fix for the fixed 380-pixel panel and the oversized paddings that
# put the reading past the bottom and right edges.
# diagnostic: GUI-35. Where the compositor delegates decorations to the host,
# the host's own title bar and insets take 48 of the window's 240 pixels, and
# the button row is laid out below the window.
# diagnostic-on: linux
expect-onscreen #count
expect-onscreen #Increment
expect-onscreen #Decrement
expect-onscreen #Reset
